646: ## P3F.9. The resolved cusp orbit as a nodal elliptic neighbourhood times a circle
647: 
648: The local calculation giving the product is as follows. Start with the
649: ordinary conifold xy=uv, with the circle acting on u,v with weights+1,-1
650: and fixing x,y. A small resolution has charts
651: 
652:     (x,v,z),   u=xz, y=vz;
653:     (u,y,w),   x=uw, v=yw;      w=1/z.
654: 
655: The orbit charts, with the Hopf smoothing defined using these normal
656: coordinates, are
657: 
658:     (x,y,b), b=(|z|²-|v|²)/2;
659:     (x,y,b'), b'=(|u|²-|w|²)/2.
660: 
661: On the overlap r=|z|²>0 they satisfy
662: 
663:     2b=r-|y|²/r,       2b'=|x|²r-1/r,
664:     db'/db=(|x|²+r^(-2))/(1+|y|²r^(-2))>0.       (P3F.9.1)
665: 
666: Thus projection to(x,y) is a smooth submersion with oriented
667: one-dimensional fibres. Every fibre is a line: away from(x,y)=(0,0)
668: the two charts join its negative and positive ends in the displayed
669: increasing order; over(0,0) the exceptional interval joins the two
670: half-lines. A smooth section can be chosen in the free part. For
671: epsilon>0 choose the unique r>0 solving
672: 
673:     |x|²r-|y|²/r+2epsilon(r-1)/(r+1)=0.
674: 
675: The left side increases strictly from a negative to a positive value;
676: its derivative is |x|²+|y|²/r²+4epsilon/(r+1)²>0. Consequently r is a
677: smooth positive function of(x,y), and the representatives
678: z=sqrt(r),v=y/sqrt(r),u=x sqrt(r) give the section in the orbit.
679: A positive vertical vector field, patched by a partition of unity and
680: rescaled to be complete, identifies each line with R by flow from this
681: section. It therefore gives a product diffeomorphism over C².
682: 
683: This comparison can be made relative to a prescribed product
684: identification outside the node neighbourhood. The quotient smoothing
685: uses a choice of invariant metric in the fixed normal bundle; choose
686: it to agree with the original product normal metric outside that
687: neighbourhood. There projection to(x,y) is the original smooth
688: submersion. On overlapping local line trivialisations the transitions
689: are increasing by(P3F.9.1). Taking a partition of unity on the base and
690: a convex combination of increasing, proper fibre coordinates produces
691: an increasing proper coordinate agreeing with the prescribed one where
